    "q-87241": {
      "dom_id": "step-q87241",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}k{e}^{10x},\\, & x<0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "For a function $f(x)$ defined on a set $S$ to be a valid probability density function, it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nIn our case, for the function $f(x)=k{e}^{10x}$ on the interval $-\\infty <x<0,$ the second condition states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}k{e}^{10x}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}k{e}^{10x}\\,\\text{d}x={[\\frac{k}{10}{e}^{10x}]}_{-\\infty }^{0}=\\frac{k}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this result back into the first equation and solving for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{k}{10}=1\\,⟹\\,k=10.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
